# The append is stamped with the author's epoch when it is sent, not when the
# write was admitted, so a write admitted before the close carries the
# re-claimed epoch and is accepted above the recorded head.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestStampAtAppend
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the foreign append carries the author's current epoch instead of the epoch it was admitted under
PERTURBS: ForeignAlloc, ForeignReject

--- FIND
    /\ fpend
    /\ fstamp >= fFence
--- REPLACE
    /\ fpend
\* MUTATION: stamped at append time.
    /\ fEpoch >= fFence
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ fpend
    /\ fstamp < fFence
--- REPLACE
    /\ fpend
    /\ fEpoch < fFence
--- END
